From: FFMake knowledge base <ffmake@local>
Subject: avfilter/vf_libopencv: port to the OpenCV 4 C++ API

OpenCV 4 removed the C runtime this filter was written against: the
headers hard-require C++11 and cvSmooth/cvDilate/cvErode and friends
are gone, so neither the C probe nor the C filter body can work with
OpenCV 4. Restructure in two halves:

  - vf_libopencv.c keeps the filter registration (AVOption/pads use
    designated initializers, a C-only construct) and loses every
    OpenCV include; it forwards to extern "C" core hooks;
  - ocv_core.cpp carries the OpenCV logic on the C++ API: zero-copy
    cv::Mat striding over the AVFrame buffers, cv::dilate/erode with
    anchored cv::MorphTypes, cvSmooth modes mapped to cv::blur /
    cv::medianBlur / cv::GaussianBlur / cv::bilateralFilter
    (blur_no_scale has no OpenCV 4 equivalent and is approximated with
    the normalized blur), cvCreateStructuringElementEx mapped to
    cv::getStructuringElement with custom shapes built from the values
    file as a CV_8U kernel.

The ocv user interface (filter_name/filter_params and the dilate,
erode, smooth sub-filter option syntax) is unchanged. Private state is
held by C++ objects behind the opaque core pointer.

